WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.900
Vertex AI.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.763
If an employer runs on Google Cloud, this is where their AI work lives.

3
00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:08.433
Let's see its three faces.

4
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:13.067
Vertex AI is GCP's machine learning platform.

5
00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:17.133
It is the analogue of SageMaker, and the front door to Gemini.

6
00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:20.433
If a job post says Vertex, this is what they mean.

7
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:23.200
Vertex has three faces.

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.588
The Model Garden is a catalog of foundation and open models.

9
00:00:27.588 --> 00:00:31.267
You can browse, deploy, or call them, Gemini included.

10
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.644
Pipelines are managed, versioned training workflows.

11
00:00:34.644 --> 00:00:37.367
Think Airflow, but for machine learning steps.

12
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:43.533
And Endpoints put your model behind an autoscaling URL, just like SageMaker endpoints.

13
00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:48.167
For LLM work, the day-one skill is structured output.

14
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.933
You pass a prompt together with a response schema.

15
00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:54.467
Gemini replies with JSON that matches the schema.

16
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:59.133
It parses into a typed object, instead of prose you would have to regex.

17
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:01.367
Here is the code.

18
00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:06.967
First, a Pydantic class describes the shape we want: an event type and a severity.

19
00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.667
The client is created with Vertex turned on.

20
00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:13.500
We call generate content, and pass the schema in the config.

21
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.433
Then we validate the reply into the class, and get a typed event.

22
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:20.267
Here is a portfolio move.

23
00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:27.300
A prospective employer runs everything on GCP, and their LLM feature is Gemini through Vertex.

24
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.233
You port one agent tool, the space-weather summarizer, to Vertex using the response schema.

25
00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:35.594
Same agent, different front door.

26
00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:40.900
In the interview you compare Bedrock and Vertex from experience, not from blog posts.

27
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.026
Let's recap.

28
00:01:43.026 --> 00:01:46.500
Vertex AI is GCP's machine learning platform.

29
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.500
Its three faces are Model Garden, Pipelines, and Endpoints.

30
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.267
The day-one skill is calling Gemini with a response schema.

31
00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:57.300
That gives you a typed object, not prose.

32
00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.233
Next up: Azure core services.
